# Drafted by Gemini (R26 Brimstone Behemoth), edited. The Brimstone Behemoth: hook, clues, weakness, the lair fight and the aftermath.

~ arrive
set mf_behemoth_arrived
cutscene mf_rowans_erupts
Narrator: Rowan's Rise splits open like an old boil, spilling red light down its flank while the surrounding heather turns to grey ash.
cutscene mf_rowans_erupts_2
Narrator: Winged shapes haul themselves up from the rivers of slag, beating heavy through a sky the colour of a three-day bruise.
cutscene end
Narrator: The burst hill smokes over a mile of cinders, and down in the camp the faithful have hung their tents with strips of red rag.
check Dexterity DC 20 -> arrive_ok | arrive_hit

~ arrive_ok
Narrator: {name} drops flat behind a split boulder as a falling stone roars past, leaving the smell of scorched hair and hot iron on the wind.
set mf_behemoth_resisted
-> END

~ arrive_hit
Narrator: A white-hot stone shatters against the turf beside {name}, and the stray cinders bite deep into their sleeve before they can roll clear.
damage 4d10 fire party
-> END

~ region
Narrator: Your boots sink ankle-deep in warm soot as you cross the moor, while burning stones drop whistling from the low red clouds.
time +60
check Dexterity DC 20 -> arrive_ok | arrive_hit

~ hook
mf_ash_cultist [smile]: The hill has opened at last, just as the old verses promised it would. Come sit by the braziers, friends, and take a good seat for the end of all things.
set mf_behemoth_asked
quest mf_behemoth asked
-> menu

~ hook_again
mf_ash_cultist [smile]: It will not be long now, you can feel the heat of it through your soles. Have you changed your minds, then, about joining us in the last prayer?
-> menu

~ menu
* Ask what has been happening -> trouble
* Ask where it comes from -> where
* [if not flag.mf_behemoth_found] Ask how to find it -> route_a
* Say we will deal with it -> END

~ trouble
mf_ash_cultist [afraid]: The sky throws down its stones every hour on the bell, and our brothers pop like dry pine needles in a hearth. Whoever the fire only grazes wakes up changed, and not for the better.
-> menu

~ where
mf_ash_cultist [sad]: That thing in the pit was born from every old tale of the world's end, called up by the spiteful ghost of little Rowan. She hated the whole living realm and wished it all to cinders.
-> menu

~ route_a
mf_ash_cultist [sly]: If you mean tospoil our great night, look to the girl's spirit first. Dig up the plain truth of her wickedness and cast it in her teeth, and her pet beast will lose its stomach.
* [Persuasion DC 20] Learn the truth of Rowan's wickedness -> a_ok | a_slow
* [Intimidation DC 20] Press her story until she admits it -> a_ok | a_slow
* Gather every tale of Rowan, however long it takes -> a_slow
* Another time -> menu

~ a_ok
mf_ash_cultist [neutral]: So you pieced her sordid little history together, did you? Proud as a queen and twice as cruel, longing for the sky to fall, with never a soft thought save for her sister.
time +60
set mf_behemoth_found
set mf_behemoth_clue_a
quest mf_behemoth trail
-> menu

~ a_slow
Narrator: It takes hours of coaxing dry memories from old folk and squinting at faded ink, until the shape of Rowan's short, bitter life lies plain before you.
time +300
set mf_behemoth_found
quest mf_behemoth trail
-> menu

~ clue
mf_rowan_spirit [angry]: You have come a long way through the soot for nothing, strangers, because you are far too late. The end is already here, and I was only the first honest soul to ask for it.
set mf_behemoth_clue_met
-> clue_menu

~ clue_again
mf_rowan_spirit [neutral]: Back again through the cinders, are you? Speak quickly if you have anything left to say, before the mountain finishes clearing its throat.
-> clue_menu

~ clue_menu
* Ask about it -> clue_talk
* [if not flag.mf_behemoth_found] Ask how to find it -> route_b
* [if flag.mf_behemoth_found and not flag.mf_behemoth_weak] Ask what could hurt it -> weak
* Take our leave -> END

~ clue_talk
mf_rowan_spirit [sad]: I will not play penitent for you: I was wicked to the marrow, and I wanted this dirty world scrubbed out. Only my sister Clara ever kept my hand from the match.
-> clue_menu

~ route_b
mf_rowan_spirit [sad]: Do not look at me with those wet eyes, I asked for no pity. Tell me one thing only, and be plain about it: did my sister ever have children of her own?
* [Arcana DC 20] Find Rowan's sister's descendant in the camp -> b_ok | b_slow
* [History DC 20] Trace the family line from the barrow's portrait -> b_ok | b_slow
* Search the camp for anyone with her sister's eyes -> b_slow
* Another time -> clue_menu

~ b_ok
mf_rowan_spirit [smile]: Step closer to the embers and let me look at your face, girl. You have Clara's eyes down to the very squint, and I see my name is not quite dead on your tongue.
time +60
set mf_behemoth_found
set mf_behemoth_clue_b
quest mf_behemoth trail
-> clue_menu

~ b_slow
Narrator: You go from tent to tent through the drifting ash, asking quiet questions of frightened folk, until at last you find one who carries her sister's blood.
time +300
set mf_behemoth_found
quest mf_behemoth trail
-> clue_menu

~ weak
mf_rowan_spirit [sad]: The beast down there wears my spite like a coat of iron. If I walk into the pit of my own free will, the fire that feeds it will turn and scald its belly instead.
* [Persuasion DC 20] Persuade Rowan to go willingly into the lava -> weak_ok | weak_slow
* [Insight DC 20] Show her the sister's love and let her choose -> weak_ok | weak_slow
* Sit with her through the long hour until she is ready -> weak_slow
* Another time -> clue_menu

~ weak_ok
mf_rowan_spirit [sad]: Clara, she used to hold my wrist just so when the temper took me. Stand back from the rim now, all of you, while I go down and put my house in order.
time +60
give mf_rowan_locket
set mf_behemoth_weak
quest mf_behemoth ready
-> clue_menu

~ weak_slow
Narrator: You sit beside the quiet girl while the ash settles on your shoulders for a long, wordless hour, until at last she stands and brushes her skirt.
time +300
give mf_rowan_locket
set mf_behemoth_weak
quest mf_behemoth ready
-> clue_menu

~ lair
Narrator: The cracked lip of the crater glows dull orange ahead of you, the heat wavering like summer glass as something vast shifts in the molten stone below.
* Go in and face it -> fight
* Not yet -> END

~ fight
cutscene mf_behemoth_reveals
Narrator: The Brimstone Behemoth hauls its bulk over the crater's rim, a mountain of blackened horn and Split stone with wings of greasy smoke blotting out the stars.
cutscene mf_behemoth_reveals_2
Narrator: It wastes no breath on boasts or curses, only opens its furnace jaws until the whole grey moor glares bright as noon.
cutscene end
if flag.mf_behemoth_weak
combat mf_behemoth_weak
elif level >= 20
combat mf_behemoth_full
else
combat mf_behemoth_light
endif

~ aftermath
cutscene mf_behemoth_falls
Narrator: The great beast gutters like a tallow candle in a draught, sliding back into the cooling slag as the bruised sky above the hill begins to clear.
cutscene mf_behemoth_falls_2
Narrator: High overhead, the Crooked Moon has stopped its slow turn away from the earth. It hangs low above the chimney pots now, staring straight down at you with a wide, patient smile.
cutscene end
set mf_behemoth_aftermath
set old_fears_slain += 1
set moonfall_credit += 1
set moonfall_nights_left += 1
give hide_of_the_brimstone_behemoth
quest mf_behemoth slain
quest moonfall one_last_choice
Narrator: The eighth and last of the Old Fears lies cold in the ash, and up in the quiet sky the moon waits for you alone.
move mf_last_hill:from_rise

~ descendant
marianna_grey [afraid]: Rowan... I do not know why that name comes to my mouth so easily, truly I don't. My mother's people never spoke it inside the house, not once while I was growing.
* Tell her about Rowan -> descendant_told
* Ask her what she remembers -> descendant_memory
* Leave her be -> END

~ descendant_memory
marianna_grey [sad]: My grandmother would always set her mending down in her lap when the dusk came on. She used to stare out the parlour window toward that hill for the longest time, and never said why.
-> descendant

~ descendant_told
marianna_grey [sad]: Oh, the poor, bitter creature, to carry such a coal in her chest for all those years. I will go up the hill to her, if you think she would bear to look at me.
set mf_behemoth_descendant
advantage persuasion 2h: Rowan's sister's blood stands beside you
-> END
